= Introduction — Wave 1.5

The Alliance held. Your network of marriages, trade routes, and whispered promises has become something real — something with weight. Lords answer your summons. The merchant guilds of the western cities route their caravans through your territory because it is safer than the alternatives. When you speak in a war council, the room listens before deciding.

But you have also learned that Calradia rewards the adaptable. The continent does not care about your plans. It throws famines, plagues, unexpected wars, and the sudden death of key allies at you without warning. A ruler who cannot pivot dies. A ruler who has only one way of fighting, one way of making money, one way of managing vassals — that ruler becomes a cautionary tale that other lords tell their children.

This is the wave where you stop being merely competent and start being dangerous. Your army is no longer a collection of whatever recruits you could find. It is a war machine with doctrine. Your economy is no longer a trickle of workshop income and tournament bets. It is a system — supply lines, agricultural estates, recovered battlefield loot. Your companions are no longer just extra swords. They command their own parties with purpose, patrol your territory, and handle problems before they reach your attention.

The mods in Wave 1.5 are not light tweaks. They are medium-weight system changers. Each one makes a meaningful difference in how you play. Together, they transform Bannerlord from a game about running around Calradia hitting things into a game about ruling Calradia with strategy.

== Wave 1.5 Objectives

+ *Take command of the campaign map.* Your companion parties patrol intelligently. Enemy AI no longer wanders aimlessly — it defends, attacks, and surrenders based on realistic calculation. Your army has supply lines. Your garrisons train and recruit autonomously. You are no longer doing everything yourself.

+ *Build a kingdom that functions without you.* Diplomacy matters. Vassalage has ceremony and consequence. Execution carries weight. Politics follows logic rather than random number generators. You can swear fealty, challenge for thrones, or build from nothing — but every path has rules now.

+ *Develop your character and dynasty meaningfully.* Detailed creation gives you a character that is truly yours. Your spouse, children, and companions have depth beyond stat blocks. Your heirs matter. Your legacy extends beyond your own death.

+ *Expand your tactical options.* Battle duels, naval combat, stealth assassinations, soldier enlistment — these are not flavor. They are genuine alternative ways to achieve your goals that sit alongside the traditional army-vs-army approach.

+ *Prepare for the Reckoning.* Wave 2's heavy overhauls will fundamentally transform Calradia's map, factions, economy, and diplomacy. Wave 1.5 gets you ready — your systems are robust, your character is developed, and your playstyle has adapted to a more complex game.
